Date: Thu, 8 Apr 93 03:52:29 -0700
From: mcpherso@lumina.ucsd.edu (John McPherson)
Subject: FAQs

Hello Extropians,

   I'm a recently returned semi-lurker (I post only occassionally),
and I have two FAQs.

1. Is there an Extropian FAQ available?

2. What are the rough priorities of the group?  There is quite
   a variety of interests and endeavors relevant to the group,
   but I'm curious to know if some developments are more urgent
   than others.  Here's a brief outline that I threw together
   in an attempt to broadly classify extropian concerns:

-----------------------

A. Personal Immortality
   a. Life Extension
   b. Cryonic Preservation
   c. Nanotech Restoration
   d. Uploading

B. Maximum Socio-economic Freedom
   a. Libertarianism (minarchy, free-market, jury nullification,
         constitutionally-limited government)
   b. Voluntarism (peaceful anarchy, complete laissez faire,
         spontaneous order unleashed)
   c. Privately Produced Law, TAZs, etc.

C. Maximum Technological Access
   a. Private Electronic Communications (PGP, anonymous remailers)
   b. Hypertext / Hypermedia
   c. Virtual Reality
   d. Personal Factories (nanotech?)

D. Optimal Self-Transformation
   a. Intelligence and Aptitude Raising
   b. Attitude Improving
   c. Mastery of Particular Knowledge and Skills 

E. Space Activities
   a. High Orbital Mini-Earths
   b. Colonization (Luna, Mars, etc.)
   c. Industrialization
   d. Star Travel

F. Meetings
   a. Parties, Social Events
   b. Conferences, Seminars

   I guess my question could be rephrased as "If you could have
one of the above, now, which would you pick?"

   I know this listing is far from complete, so please feel free to
add to it, correct it, trash it, or draft a better one.

   Given this list, at first glance I would probably choose 
"personal immortality" as my top priority, then "intelligence 
raising", and then "maximum socio-economic freedom".
   You'll probably all see where I'm going with this ... the
formation of special-interest task groups to focus on particular
priorities, and to achieve them.


